msgid "Build a graph from a folder with StratiMiner"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Build a graph from a folder of sources through a table you can open and "
"check.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Excavation diaries, reports, lists of units: when a study has its sources"
" but no graph yet, **StratiMiner** builds one. It works in two halves "
"joined by a table. The first half produces ``em_data.xlsx``, the table of"
" the Extended Matrix with its sheets of units, epochs and claims; you can"
" write it by hand, or have an AI model draft it from the folder of "
"sources. The second half turns the table into a graph, always in the same"
" way: the same table gives the same graph. The AI writes only the table, "
"which you open and correct before anything enters a graph."
msgstr ""

msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"StratiMiner needs no open graph. To draft the table with AI, an AI "
"provider and its key must be set in ``Settings ▸ Advanced`` (see "
":doc:`/reference/settings`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Open StratiMiner"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Choose ``Tools ▸ StratiMiner``. With nothing open, the empty canvas "
"offers the same panel through the link **build one from your sources**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The StratiMiner window: how the em_data.xlsx table is made, by hand or "
"with the AI, and the Graph creator that turns it into an em.json."
msgstr ""

msgid "The panel asks first **How do you have the em_data.xlsx table?**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**I make it by hand**: fill the sheets yourself, then go to :ref"
":`stratiminer-graph-creator`."
msgstr ""

msgid "**I generate it with the AI, from messy data**: follow the steps below."
msgstr ""

msgid "Draft the table with AI"
msgstr ""

msgid "In **Source folder**, give the folder that holds the sources."
msgstr ""

msgid "Desktop"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Press **…** and choose the folder in the system dialog: its full path is "
"filled in."
msgstr ""

msgid "Web"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Press **…** to choose the folder: the browser gives only its name. "
"Complete the field with the full path of the folder as EMStudio's service"
" sees it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In **Output language**, write the language the table should be written "
"in, or leave the field empty to keep the language of each source."
msgstr ""

msgid "Choose one of the two ways."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Generate em_data.xlsx (AI)**: EMStudio's service sends the sources to "
"the AI model and writes the workbook. It reads text files, and PDFs that "
"carry a text layer; it always lists the files it could not read, and why."
" A scanned PDF without text is reported as such."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Copy prompt for Cowork**: the prompt is copied, to be run in a Cowork "
"session that can read the folder. This is the way for scans and for every"
" file the first way reports as unread. When the browser refuses the "
"clipboard, the prompt appears in a field below, with **Save the prompt to"
" a file…**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When the AI way has finished, the path of the new ``em_data.xlsx`` is "
"already in the field of the **Graph creator**. Open the workbook in your "
"spreadsheet program and review it: the units, their epochs, the relations"
" between them."
msgstr ""

msgid "Turn the table into a graph"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Under **Graph creator · em_data.xlsx → em.json**, give the path of the "
"table, or press **…** to choose it."
msgstr ""

msgid "The system dialog fills in the real path of the workbook."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The chosen workbook is copied to EMStudio's service, and the field "
"receives the path of that copy."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Press **Transform into em.json**. The **Mapping editor** opens with the "
"table as its source, read as **None: an EM table**, with **A new graph** "
"and **Written into the graph** chosen. A line at the top says that the "
"rows are **StratiMiner's proposals**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Press **Apply** (see :doc:`read-a-table-through-a-mapping` for the other "
"choices of that window)."
msgstr ""

msgid "What you get"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The graph opens as a new graph in the workspace, beside the graphs "
"already open, named after the workbook. The **Log** sums up what the "
"table produced and lists its warnings. The data drafted by AI stay among "
"the warnings of the graph until a person verifies them, so the review "
"continues inside EMStudio."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Save the graph with ``File ▸ Save as…`` to give it its em.json. The "
"source folder and the table stay where they are, and you can run "
"StratiMiner again on a corrected table."
msgstr ""

msgid "See also"
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`read-a-table-through-a-mapping`, for the Mapping editor."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`/how-to/stratigraphy/check-the-chronology`, to check the epochs of "
"the new graph."
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`/how-to/narrative/ai-drafts`, for the other use of AI in EMStudio."
msgstr ""

